WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:01.715
Where the first galaxies are now.

00:02.495 --> 00:09.041
The James Webb telescope has seen galaxies whose light left when the universe was about three hundred million years old.

00:09.593 --> 00:15.328
Those galaxies are now about 34 billion light-years away, in a few small patches of our sky.

00:15.952 --> 00:17.580
None is drawn on this map.
